# Phase 46 (Property Intelligence: Address Normalization & Google
# Integration). BROWSER-restricted key only -- a public identifier by
# design (restrict it by HTTP referrer + to Maps JavaScript API/Places API
# (New) in Google Cloud Console), never the backend's server key. Leave
# blank until Google Cloud access exists; the address-autocomplete widget
# safely degrades to plain manual entry with this unset (see
# src/config/googleMaps.js). Once set for a deployed environment, also set
# the backend's GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY_CONFIGURED=true so the sanitized
# public config endpoint can advertise autocomplete availability.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=
